<h2>Cupfection or Blizzard?</h2><p>If you like every bite to taste the same, get a Blizzard such as the <a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard">Choco Brownie Extreme</a>. If you like distinct layers of brownie, cookie and fudge, the Cupfection is for you. It is big, at about 720 calories, so it shares well.</p><p>See every cone, sundae and novelty on the <a href="/categories/classic-treats">classic treats menu</a>.</p><h2>Good to know</h2><ul><li>It is one of the most expensive single treats at DQ, at about $6.29.</li><li>Ask for an extra spoon; it is big enough for two.</li><li>Some stores rotate Cupfection flavors, so check what is on the board.</li></ul><p>For a cheaper layered treat, the <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a> costs about $4.99.</p>
